# Protocol invariants

- No instruction may send user or treasury assets to a team, creator, founder, or admin address. Destinations are fixed in code or by supermajority governance.
- Rounding always favors the protocol, never the user.
- A cToken's backing-per-token never falls after any operation.
- Exactly one mint path: a registered EOL Token, into its own treasury. No admin mint.
- cToken transfers fail at Token-2022 (NonTransferable), not in our logic.
- Redemption never closes, on either token type.
- Every backing / ratio / reserve-mint trigger **counts unconverted USDC**. Missing it reports a healthy launch as unbacked.
- Launches validate against **snapshotted** params, never live governance numbers.
- A missing governance result is an error, never silent consent.

```rust
// ❌ BAD — day-one false alarm
let backing = csol_balance;

// ✅ GOOD
let backing = csol_balance.saturating_add(unconverted_usdc_in_sol_terms);
```
